## 12. ACHIEVEMENT UNLOCK ENGINE

Build reliable, deterministic unlock processing.

Required behavior:

1. Receive a verified completion event or updated student progress state.
2. Evaluate relevant achievement requirements.
3. Check whether the achievement is already unlocked.
4. Unlock it only when the condition is satisfied.
5. Store the achievement ID and timestamp.
6. Update collection progress.
7. Trigger a celebration notification when appropriate.
8. Prevent duplicate unlock records.
9. Evaluate dependent achievements after prerequisite unlocks.

Examples:

Mark NT as Explored → Peridot's Protocol

Complete first valid CTRL Quiz → First Spark

Complete a comparison of two tracks → Fusion Theory

Unlock four prerequisite NT achievements → Techno-Gem

Unlock 10 distinct achievements → Crystal Collector

Unlock all 15 track achievements → Your Own Universe

Ensure dependent achievements can unlock correctly when multiple conditions become true during one update.

Prevent infinite achievement evaluation loops.

